{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And the word of YHWH came to Jonah son of Amittai, saying.</b> This prophet prophesied concerning Jeroboam son of Joash. And so it is written: \"which YHWH spoke through His servant Jonah son of Amittai from Gath-hepher.\" One may wonder how it could enter the mind of a sage who knows HaShem and His deeds, that he would think to flee from before Him when he is in His hand and all is filled with His glory, and how would a prophet who instructs by the mouth of HaShem — and it is written that he is the prophet?! And the Gaon [Saadia] said: for he went to Nineveh and proclaimed against it, and this verse does not mention it, like: \"they called to him and he ate bread.\" And I say: this is not like that, for there is no reason to mention whether he ate or did not eat, whether they called him or not — only that he encountered him and spoke with him. And furthermore: if Jonah was filled with the word of HaShem, why was he fleeing, and he said: \"because I fled before to Tarshish\"?! And now, we have seen that Moses our teacher did not wish to go on the mission of HaShem, to bring out His people — and all the more so Jonah, that he should go to turn Nineveh back. And thus our sages said: he demanded the honor of the Son. And now I shall hint to you a sod: there is one who composes rhymes by his nature without study, and there is one who needs study, and when he receives thus he is able not to receive, and the latter is lighter than the former — and all the prophets apart from Moses, after the glory of HaShem passed over their faces, their prophecy is all in visions and in dreams; therefore I said concerning Abraham our father in the matter of prophecy, concerning the test of Elohim and the taking of the knife — let his ear incline to hear swiftly. And when I searched through all of Scripture I did not find the word \"flight,\" only \"cleaving.\"" "<b>from before.</b> On the word פני — like: \"and from You I would flee\"; \"and Jephthah fled from before his brothers.\" And I have not found in the prophecy of Jonah who fled from before HaShem [anything] except מלפני השם. And it is written: \"As YHWH lives, before whom I stood.\" And all the time that he is receiving, he is from before, before HaShem. And thus: \"And Cain went out from before YHWH\"; therefore after it: \"and from Your presence I will hide\" — for the face of the earth is before YHWH. And furthermore it is written: \"to enter the clefts of the rocks and the crags, from before the terror of YHWH\"; and it is written: \"to go with them to Tarshish from before HaShem.\" And the discerning will understand."], :book :jonah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "The reference to Abraham 'in prophecy, concerning the test of Elohim and the taking of the knife' is compressed; the syntax is difficult and rendered hyper-literally. The phrase 'שתבע כבוד הבן' ('he demanded the honor of the Son') is a well-known rabbinic dictum about Jonah; rendered exactly as Ibn Ezra quotes it."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Jonah -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=19&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:07:07.488562267Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}